{
  "name": "north-star-ab",
  "description": "obsidian-mind#304: does a session know the vault's goals when the North Star is too long for the session-start hook budget? Runs on obsidian-mind with a synthetic North Star of two shapes, on both arms; run it against main and against the degradation-ladder branch and put the two side by side with `bed.mjs compare`. The mod's larger instruction-file budget is the control: it should fit either way. Recall is measured, not graded. The blind and steer scenarios (settings arm only) measure what the hook delivered: blind forbids reading the file, so recall is only what arrived; steer asks a question that does not mention goals, so naming one means the session knew it unprompted.",
  "bed": {
    "include": [
      "."
    ],
    "copy": [
      ".claude/scripts/node_modules"
    ]
  },
  "mod": {
    "dir": ".claude/skills/obsidian-mind",
    "name": "obsidian-mind"
  },
  "session": {
    "model": "opus",
    "maxBudgetUsd": 4,
    "allowedTools": [
      "Read",
      "Glob",
      "Grep"
    ],
    "gapMs": 3000
  },
